      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-06-01_WidnesExaminer_art0088" n="art0088">
        <head>VOLUNTEER ENCAMPMENT</head>
        <p>THE VOLUNTEER ENCAMPMENT</p>
        <p>Our local Volunteers will enter brigade camp at Con- way to-day (Saturday). The following instructions appear in the battalion orders for the current week .. The battalion will parade in marching order (with kersey frocks and helmets),water bottles and haversacks at the Drill Hall, at 8 o.en. and proceed by the London and North-Weatern Railway to Conway, there to ba encamped till the 17th June. Men who cannot parade on Saturday may folow on Monday, in which case tickets can be obtained at the Drill Hall. The armoury will be opened one hour b .fsre parade for issue of rifles. The baggage guard under the command of 2nd Lieutenant H G Roberts will parade at the Drill Hall, at 7-30 p.m, All heavy baggage of Offic.rs and N.C.O.'s must be placed in the Drill Hall by 3 p.m. and no heavy baggage can be taken with the Battalion. N.C.O.'s and men being provided with valises, no tin boxes, Sz , will be allowed to be taken, exlept cma Calour Sergeant's Balt per C,m- pany for stationery, Sza. These must be at the Drill Hall by 6 p.m. on Satorday. All Offi3era' Haze age must be ls belled with the owner's name and be depotd at the Dr;11. Hall by 6 p.m. Officore chargers and bicycles of the Cyclist Company to be at Bank Quay Station by 5 p.m. All members attend- ing camp must provide themselves with the following articles, viz. :—Towels, soap, rsz)r. blacking brushes, comb and brush, button brass, knife, fork, spoon, sponge, pipe clay, Sz t. They are also venial- mended to provide themselves with two grey flannel shirts and two pairs of boots. All spare Wt tunics, etc , taken to camp this year will be carried in kit begs which have been provided for each man and which will henceforth be considered as part of his egnipment for wlath he will be liable to make good any Is as or dsmage except by fair wear. The field kit will ho carried in the valise as usual. Nothing but kit have will be allowed to convoy spare kits in to camp. Tare A'IVRTICPea party, consisting of Qaartermaater Ser-?eant J Willcocki, Arrnourer Sergeant G Davies, Ser- geant T whitfi .Id and 15 rank and file, under the com- mand of 21d Lieutenant CL Williamson and Quarter- maater A F G Potter left Warrington for Conway on Wednesday. Toe transp )rt sn'isn followed on Thurslay morning</p>
        <p>CYCLES.—BARGAINS.-1,500 Machines, new &amp;second-hand, from 80s. each ; agents wanted ' • wholesale list free any address. Warrelow &amp; Company, Weston-super-Mare. NEW RAPID CYCLES with 81n cranks and free wheels, J. S. GAlms.sn, Cycle Factors, Bridge-st., Warrington, BEST BOOTS Fe ALL, UNDER TIIR CLOCK.— vt LATEST DESIGNS and cllourings in Prints. Muslins anti ZElriers, for summer, also a choice assortment of Sunshades just received.—W. T. WILLIAMS, 74, Sankey- stmt and 1, Leah-street, Warrington. PRE 41Eit OYCLE3 price £9 175 63.-3. S. GARLAND, Cycle Factor, Bridge-street, Warrington. ASK for CUNNINGHAM'S HIGH-CLASS MINERAL WATSRS.—Advt.</p>
